hub.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T08:22:40Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T08:22:40Z","body":"Would this not remove the ability to parse YAML? \r\n\r\nIIRC, it was this way because YAML is a superset of JSON, so if you write it in YAML or JSON, then the yaml parser can do it, but the JSON parser probably cannot?\r\n\r\nThat said, we can mark the changelog with breaking and change it to only support JSON.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3244312333/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3244445035","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2756#issuecomment-3244445035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2756","id":3244445035,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887BYk1r","user":{"login":"liuxocakn","id":166280047,"node_id":"U_kgDOCek7bw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166280047?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn","html_url":"https://github.com/liuxocakn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T09:01:43Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T09:01:43Z","body":"> Would this not remove the ability to parse YAML?\r\n> \r\n> IIRC, it was this way because YAML is a superset of JSON, so if you write it in YAML or JSON, then the yaml parser can do it, but the JSON parser probably cannot?\r\n> \r\n> That said, we can mark the changelog with breaking and change it to only support JSON.\r\n\r\nI'm not quite sure about the compatibility of YAML with JSON, but when I deployed my own project using the version from a month ago and the latest Headscale mainline version, I encountered a YAML parsing issue: InsecureForTests should have been parsed as true, but it was parsed as false, which led me to suspect for a while that it was a problem with my deployment or that headscale forced the local configuration not to set InsecureForTests to true for security reasons.\r\n\r\nAfter I reviewed the source code, I found that the tags in the DERPNode type definition do not have YAML but only JSON, and its source code is not in headscale. Therefore, I personally suggest that only supporting json parsing is more appropriate for maintenance and consistency. So this is my idea for patch! Of course, this is just my personal opinion.\r\n\r\nRegarding the issue of YAML parsing DERPNode, separate code can be written for verification. When there is only the main function, only the yaml file of DERPNode is parsed, and the same version of go as headscale is used, problems will occur: The three bool type variables STUNOnly, InsecureForTests, and CanPort80 will be parsed incorrectly, while STUNOnly will occasionally be parsed successfully（the other variables have been correctly parsed）.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3244445035/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"liuxocakn","id":166280047,"node_id":"U_kgDOCek7bw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/166280047?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn","html_url":"https://github.com/liuxocakn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liuxocakn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3468759935","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2756#issuecomment-3468759935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2756","id":3468759935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887OwRN_","user":{"login":"ArcticLampyrid","id":9017609,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMTc2MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9017609?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid","html_url":"https://github.com/ArcticLampyrid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArcticLampyrid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-30T16:01:05Z","updated_at":"2025-10-30T16:01:05Z","body":"Try lowercase `insecurefortests`, I remember it will work.","author_association":"CON